{
 "encounter_id": "00660",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, Mr Kowalski, forty-one, vomiting since last night, can't keep anything down, even water."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you. Mr Kowalski, I'm Dr Hughes. How many times have you been sick?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've lost count. Ten, twelve? All night, and this morning, even when it's just water. I want a drip, honestly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll get to that. When did it start?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About eight last night, after dinner. A kebab. I'm blaming the kebab."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "His wife rang ahead, she said he looked grey. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any pain in your tummy?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yeah, cramps. Across the middle, they come and go, and they're bad."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Dizzy when you stand?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yeah, a bit. I nearly fell getting out of the car."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any blood in what you've brought up, or black, coffee-ground stuff?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, just yellow stuff at the end. No blood."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever or shivers?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Not that I know of. No."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What tablets do you take?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Metformin, 500 mg, twice a day, and omeprazole, 20 mg once a day. Haven't taken them today, obviously."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Sensible not to. Any previous operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Gallbladder out, in 2015."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll do your observations, Mr Kowalski. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hurry up, please. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Blood pressure 100 over 62, pulse 112, temperature 37.4, oxygen 97 percent, respiratory rate 20.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thanks, Jenny. Your pressure's on the low side and your pulse is fast, which is the dehydration. Any breathing trouble?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, breathing's fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me feel your tummy. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ow. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your mouth is very dry, and your tummy is tender in the upper middle but soft, with no guarding.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it appendicitis? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No, that's not where it is. I think this is most likely gastroenteritis from something you ate, but I can't rule out a gallstone problem in the bile duct yet."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. What are you going to do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "First, we'll start intravenous fluids right now, so you stop drying out. Jenny, a cannula please."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "On it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd also like to send blood tests, including your kidney function and electrolytes, and a liver profile."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'd like to arrange an abdominal ultrasound, given the pain and your history."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will that be today? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If your bloods look suspicious, today. If not, tomorrow. We'll let you know. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. And can I have something for the sickness? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The nurse will bring you something once the line is in. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Thank you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When you're home, small sips of fluid, nothing greasy, and I'd like to see you again tomorrow morning to check how you're doing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Tomorrow. Fine. ~"
  }
 ],
